+> STOP. Captain's notes: non-binding. Captain writes, Captain trims. Anyone else: close this file now.
+
+# Captain Notes
+
+Binding behaviour lives in `features/todomvc.feature` and the referenced `assets/**`. History lives in git. These notes carry only what the next cycle needs.
+
+## Decisions captured
+
+- Stack: Vanilla JavaScript, no preprocessors, persists to `localStorage`. Confirmed by the user at task open.
+- Specs directory: `features/` (pinned by `README.md`; runner is Cucumber, DOM env is `happy-dom`). Feature file: `features/todomvc.feature` (28 scenario definitions, 30 runnable instances after the counter outline expands).
+- Base markup: `assets/app-template.index.html`. Keep `base.css` untouched; put overrides in `css/app.css`, minimal.
+- Persistence key: `todos-vanilla` (spec format `todos-[framework]`, framework = vanilla). Stored item shape: `id`, `title`, `completed`. Edit mode is not persisted.
+- Routing: hash routes `#/` (all, default), `#/active`, `#/completed` (`#!/` also allowed). Filter on the model; toggle `selected` on the filter links; persist active filter across reload.
+- `watchbill.json` is written and covers all 28 scenarios in eight ordered watches. No tier tags are used; all scenarios sit in the default tier.
+
+## Open questions
+
+- `RIGGING.md` and `AGENTS.md` are not yet fitted out, and no `## Methods` exist. Route to Shipwright to derive them (Cucumber `prove`/`verify`/`sweep`, `plank-join`, `hygiene`, `static`, `spec-lint`) before QM is dispatched.
+- Routing library: the spec suggests Flatiron Director from `/assets`, but it is not vendored in this tree. Confirm a minimal hand-rolled hash router is acceptable, or vendor Director.
+- Dependency install: the spec requires `todomvc-common` and `todomvc-app-css`. Confirm install at fitting out (install is Shipwright's, or Captain's on the greenfield fast path).
+
+## Next role
+
+Shipwright fits out the rigging, then QM runs this watchbill with a clean context. Context MUST clear before QM.
