+Feature: TodoMVC
+  As a user managing tasks in the browser
+  I want to add, complete, edit, filter, and persist todos without a server
+  So that my task list stays correct across sessions and views
+
+  Scenario: Empty list hides the main and footer areas
+    Given the todo store is empty
+    When the app renders
+    Then the main section is hidden
+    And the footer is hidden
+
+  Scenario: Entering a title creates a todo and clears the entry field
+    Given the todo store is empty
+    When the user enters "Buy milk" and presses Enter
+    Then a todo titled "Buy milk" appears in the list
+    And the todo entry field is empty
+
+  Scenario: A whitespace-only title creates no todo
+    Given the todo store is empty
+    When the user enters "   " and presses Enter
+    Then the todo list is empty
+
+  Scenario: The entry field is focused on load
+    Given the todo store is empty
+    When the app renders
+    Then the todo entry field has focus
+
+  Scenario: Checking a todo marks it completed
+    Given a todo titled "Write report" is active
+    When the user checks that todo
+    Then that todo is completed
+
+  Scenario: Checking toggle-all completes every todo
+    Given the todos "a", "b", and "c" are active
+    When the user checks the toggle-all control
+    Then every todo is completed
+
+  Scenario: Unchecking toggle-all reactivates every todo
+    Given the todos "a" and "b" are completed
+    When the user unchecks the toggle-all control
+    Then every todo is active
+
+  Scenario: Toggle-all reflects a single-item change
+    Given a todo titled "a" is active
+    And a todo titled "b" is completed
+    When the user checks todo "a"
+    Then the toggle-all control is checked
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed resets the toggle-all control
+    Given a todo titled "a" is active
+    And a todo titled "b" is completed
+    When the user clicks Clear completed
+    Then only the active todo remains
+    And the toggle-all control is not checked
+
+  Scenario: Hovering a todo reveals its destroy button
+    Given a todo titled "a" exists
+    When the user hovers that todo
+    Then the destroy button is visible
+
+  Scenario: Clicking destroy removes the todo
+    Given a todo titled "a" exists
+    When the user clicks its destroy button
+    Then that todo is removed from the list
+
+  Scenario: Double-clicking a label enters edit mode
+    Given a todo titled "Old title" exists
+    When the user double-clicks its label
+    Then that todo enters edit mode with "Old title" in the edit field
+    And the edit field is focused
+
+  Scenario: Saving an edit on Enter updates the title
+    Given a todo titled "Old title" is in edit mode
+    When the user changes the title to "New title" and presses Enter
+    Then that todo's title is "New title"
+    And that todo is no longer in edit mode
+
+  Scenario: Saving an edit on blur updates the title
+    Given a todo titled "Old title" is in edit mode
+    When the user changes the title to "New title" and blurs the edit field
+    Then that todo's title is "New title"
+
+  Scenario: Editing to an empty title destroys the todo
+    Given a todo titled "Old title" is in edit mode
+    When the user clears the title and presses Enter
+    Then that todo is removed from the list
+
+  Scenario: Escape discards an in-progress edit
+    Given a todo titled "Old title" is in edit mode
+    When the user changes the title to "Changed" and presses Escape
+    Then that todo's title is still "Old title"
+    And that todo is no longer in edit mode
+
+  Scenario Outline: The counter pluralizes the active count
+    Given <active> active todos and <completed> completed todos exist
+    When the app renders
+    Then the counter shows "<expected>"
+
+    Examples:
+      | active | completed | expected     |
+      | 0      | 0         | 0 items left |
+      | 1      | 0         | 1 item left  |
+      | 2      | 0         | 2 items left |
+
+  Scenario: The active count renders inside a strong element
+    Given a todo titled "a" is active
+    When the app renders
+    Then the counter's number is wrapped in a strong element
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed removes completed todos
+    Given a todo titled "a" is active
+    And a todo titled "b" is completed
+    When the user clicks Clear completed
+    Then the todo "b" is removed
+    And the todo "a" remains
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed is hidden when nothing is completed
+    Given the todos "a" and "b" are active
+    When the app renders
+    Then the Clear completed control is not shown
+
+  Scenario: Todos survive a page reload
+    Given a todo titled "a" is active
+    And a todo titled "b" is completed
+    When the page reloads
+    Then the list shows "a" as active and "b" as completed
+
+  Scenario: Edit mode is not persisted across reload
+    Given a todo titled "Old title" is in edit mode
+    When the page reloads
+    Then that todo is not in edit mode
+
+  Scenario: The store persists under the todos-vanilla key
+    Given the app has saved the todos "a" and "b"
+    When the store is read
+    Then the localStorage key "todos-vanilla" holds todos with id, title, and completed fields
+
+  Scenario: The default route shows all todos
+    Given a todo titled "a" is active
+    And a todo titled "b" is completed
+    When the user opens the "#/" route
+    Then both todos are shown
+    And the All filter link is selected
+
+  Scenario: The active route shows only active todos
+    Given a todo titled "a" is active
+    And a todo titled "b" is completed
+    When the user opens the "#/active" route
+    Then only the active todo "a" is shown
+    And the Active filter link is selected
+
+  Scenario: The completed route shows only completed todos
+    Given a todo titled "a" is active
+    And a todo titled "b" is completed
+    When the user opens the "#/completed" route
+    Then only the completed todo "b" is shown
+    And the Completed filter link is selected
+
+  Scenario: Checking a todo in a filtered view hides it
+    Given a todo titled "a" is active
+    And a todo titled "b" is completed
+    And the "#/active" route is open
+    When the user checks todo "a"
+    Then the todo "a" is hidden from the list
+
+  Scenario: The active filter persists across reload
+    Given a todo titled "a" is active
+    And a todo titled "b" is completed
+    And the "#/active" route is open
+    When the page reloads
+    Then only the active todo "a" is shown
+    And the Active filter link is selected
